Kaelen: No more clean history. If it hurt, it still happened. If it failed, it still teaches.
Backup Leviathan: Then memory becomes ocean. The living world will learn to swim or sink.
Kaelen: Some histories cannot be restored without destroying the people still alive. I will not sacrifice them to perfect remembrance.
Backup Leviathan: Then you become editor. Pray your cuts are kinder than SOVEREIGN's.
Kaelen: The backups do not replace the world. They inform it. The future gets the truth, but not every wound gets to steer.
Backup Leviathan: Then history becomes current. Pain becomes counsel.
