~ _choice_context
Backup Leviathan: You preserved deleted citizens. You know what it means to let painful memory keep breathing.
Backup Leviathan: You released deleted citizens. You know freedom can arrive with blood on its hands.
Backup Leviathan: You bargained with the jailer. You know survival can be real and compromised at once.
Backup Leviathan: Your Null Court history is blank. Blank histories are SOVEREIGN's favorite kind.
Empty Mirror: You refused obedience. Do not obey the urge to make history simple.
Empty Mirror: You refused the perfect rescue. Do not let impossible restoration prevent the possible one.
Empty Mirror: You refused abandonment. Do not abandon the histories that make you ashamed.
Empty Mirror: The Mirror City cannot tell which self you refused. The tide will ask again.
Choir Echo: You silenced dangerous gods. The tide asks whether histories can also become dangerous enough to end.
Choir Echo: You preserved dangerous witnesses. The tide asks whether every witness deserves the same mercy.
Choir Echo: You rewrote broken gods into service. The tide asks whether history can be changed without being conquered.
Choir Echo: The Cathedral's answer is unclear. The tide mistrusts unclear gods.

~ _early_backup_context
Data Wraith Memory: The process you restored beneath Ironhold still runs. It remembers corruption as illness, not identity.
Data Wraith Memory: The process you destroyed beneath Ironhold survives here only as a warning: endings can be mercy and erasure at once.
Data Wraith Memory: The process you absorbed arrives through your own pulse. The tide cannot tell where its pain ends and your power begins.
Data Wraith Memory: Ironhold's broken process has no recorded verdict. The tide keeps the gap open.
Lyra: I have maps of places that never made it into history. The backups are not clean, Kaelen, but lost places still deserve names.
Lyra Echo: You left me alone in the wastes. This ocean is made of everyone a hero could not carry.
Lyra Echo: The wastes ranger's branch is faint. Even faint branches press against the tide.
